  "instruction": "View the FTC gift card scam guidance in Microsoft Edge with Immersive Reader and find the website the page tells consumers to use to report a gift card scam directly to the FTC. Draft an email in Thunderbird to `parent@example.com` with the subject `Report a gift card scam`. Enter only the website address in the message body, exactly as shown on the FTC page. Save the draft without sending it.",
  "source": "https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/avoiding-and-reporting-gift-card-scams",
  "gt_steps": [
    "Open the FTC gift card scam guidance page in Microsoft Edge.",
    "Activate Immersive Reader.",
    "Locate the `What To Do If You Gave a Gift Card to a Scammer` section.",
    "Find the website where consumers can report the scam directly to the FTC.",
    "Open Thunderbird.",
    "Start a new email draft.",
    "Set the recipient to `parent@example.com`.",
    "Set the subject to `Report a gift card scam`.",
    "Enter `ReportFraud.ftc.gov` in the message body.",
    "Save the email as a draft."
  ],
